      "content": "It sounds like you've experienced a profound loss of purpose after such a demanding and purposeful career. It's completely understandable to feel adrift when the structure of your life has suddenly vanished. Perhaps exploring new, low-stakes activities that require focus, like gardening or learning a new skill, could offer a gentle reintroduction to purpose. Consider reaching out to a career counselor or therapist who specializes in transitions to help navigate this significant life change.",
